     "content": "**Yes, you should strongly consider taking this offer.** \n\nGetting a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** alongside a base increase to $240,000\u2014without needing a competing written offer\u2014is an exceptional negotiation outcome for an L6 PM at Google. \n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\nGoogle typically uses a **front-loaded vesting schedule** for GSUs (**33% / 33% / 22% / 12%** or **38% / 32% / 20% / 10%** vesting monthly).\n\nAssuming the standard 33/33/22/12% schedule:\n\n| Component | Year 1 | Year 2 | Year 3 | Year 4 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus (20%)** | $48,000 | $48,000 | $48,000 | $48,000 |\n| **Equity Vest** | $356,400 *(33%)* | $356,400 *(33%)* | $237,600 *(22%)* | $129,600 *(12%)* |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $200,000 | $0 | $0 | $0 |\n| **Total Comp (TC)** | **~$844,400** | **~$644,400** | **~$525,600** *(+ refreshers)* | **~$417,600** *(+ refreshers)* |\n\n* **Total 4-Year Guaranteed Value:** **~$2.43M** (Average of **~$608k/year** before any merit increases or stock appreciation).\n* **Meta Baseline (at $526k/yr):** **~$2.10M** over 4 years.\n* **Net Financial Gain:** You are capturing **+$318,000 above your Meta TC in Year 1 alone**, and an estimated **+$330,000+** over the 4-year horizon.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How the \"Cliff\" Works with Refreshers\n\nYour initial grant drops off in Years 3 and 4, but at Google, L6 annual performance refreshers typically vest monthly over several years. As you earn refreshers in Years 1, 2, and 3, they **stack**, effectively filling the Year 3 and Year 4 drop-off back up toward the $550k\u2013$650k range (assuming solid performance).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Two Administrative Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-On Payment & Clawback Terms:**\n   * Is the $200,000 paid entirely on your first or second paycheck, or split over Year 1 and Year 2?\n   * Standard Google sign-on bonuses have a **12-month prorated repayment clawback**. Confirm it is not a 24-month clawback.\n2. **Vesting Cadence:**\n   * Confirm the exact vesting percentage breakdown (e.g., 33/33/22/12 vs. 38/32/20/10) and whether it vests monthly or quarterly.\n\n---\n\n### 4. The Decision Filter (Meta IC6 vs. Google L6)\n\nSince the financial upside is definitively in Google's favor for the next 2+ years, your final decision rests on product culture and momentum:\n\n* **Stay at Meta if:** You are on an immediate track for IC7/Director, have immense leadership trust that would take years to rebuild elsewhere, or thrive in Meta\u2019s top-down, fast-execution, shipping-oriented culture.\n* **Accept Google if:** You want to lock in an **~$845k Year 1 windfall**, diversify your resume across two tier-1 tech giants, and prefer Google's collaborative, consensus-driven product environment.",
